  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Meeting Basic Needs and Protection Outcomes for Afghans in Iran</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">This Action supports vulnerable Afghans and host community members in the provinces of Yazd, Tehran, Alborz, Khorasan Razavi, Sistan and Baluchistan. Building on the International Organization for Migration (IOM)&#x2019;s approach to deliver aid efficiently and maintain a people-centered humanitarian response, the project adopts a basic needs framework, addressing the multiple requirements of vulnerable people through an integrated and coordinated response, particularly in protracted crises. IOM is providing support to 5,000 vulnerable people to help them meet their recurrent basic needs, thereby preventing their situation from worsening and reducing the necessity for sustained assistance. IOM is also providing tailored assistance for 1,500 Afghans to address specific needs such as documentation costs, safe accommodation and disability-related requirements. This support is provided based on comprehensive case management assessments and is complemented by sustained protection services, adhering to the &apos;do no harm&apos; principles. Furthermore, IOM is conducting individual counseling on protection matters, including support for regularization processes for 1,350 Afghans and case management services for 150 Afghans. This Action includes a crisis modifier to respond promptly to sudden-onset emergencies or the worsening of existing crises. This component provides support for 2,000 individuals, including refugees and migrants in Iran.</narrative>
  </description>
